From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:58:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hw/pci-host/ppce500: rebuild the PCI windows on load

The e500 PCI controller's outbound windows (CPU address -> PCI memory)
and inbound windows (PCI address -> system memory) are memory region
aliases built by e500_update_pow/_piw when the guest writes the window
registers. The registers are migrated, but nothing rebuilds the aliases
on load, so a guest started with -loadvm (or migrated to a fresh
destination) has no outbound windows: its PCI BARs are unreachable and
the first access to a PCI device goes nowhere.

Repro: boot Linux on ppce500 with a virtio-blk-pci disk mounted, savevm,
then -loadvm in a new process and write a file to the disk: the guest
idles forever waiting for the request. (A loadvm in the same process
keeps the windows the guest built before, so it needs the host bridge
fix that follows to show.)

Rebuild every window from the loaded registers in a post_load, the same
calls the register writes make. The migration stream is unchanged.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Origin: new
---
 hw/pci-host/ppce500.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c b/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c
index 67180ba5f05078f5b5d6ebb33f0b1de36fdfa90c..b74b2649e8d5c4ec0627214ca57a211402b63c36 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c
+++ b/hw/pci-host/ppce500.c
@@ -398,10 +398,30 @@ static const VMStateDescription vmstate_pci_inbound = {
     }
 };
 
+/*
+ * The windows' memory regions are built only when the guest writes their registers. Rebuild
+ * them from the loaded registers, or a loaded guest's PCI BARs (outbound) and its devices' DMA
+ * into RAM (inbound) go nowhere.
+ */
+static int ppce500_pci_post_load(void *opaque, int version_id)
+{
+    PPCE500PCIState *pci = opaque;
+    int i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < PPCE500_PCI_NR_POBS; i++) {
+        e500_update_pow(pci, i);
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < PPCE500_PCI_NR_PIBS; i++) {
+        e500_update_piw(pci, i);
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static const VMStateDescription vmstate_ppce500_pci = {
     .name = "ppce500_pci",
     .version_id = 1,
     .minimum_version_id = 1,
+    .post_load = ppce500_pci_post_load,
     .fields = (const VMStateField[]) {
         VMSTATE_STRUCT_ARRAY(pob, PPCE500PCIState, PPCE500_PCI_NR_POBS, 1,
                              vmstate_pci_outbound, struct pci_outbound),
